                "retweet_count": 212,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Today is not a happy day for me. I am devastated at the loss of one of my dear colleagues, a young man that I considered like a son. Donald Payne Jr. was a devoted member of Congress, who despite his ongoing health struggles, worked hard for his constituents every day. Not only did he speak to them from the floor of Congress, he worked in his district to ensure that he was doing everything possible to support a fair and decent quality of life for everyone. I am going to miss him for his impressive and immaculate dress, and I'm going to miss that smile when I was so-called advising him.",
